2026-01-30 10:27:18 | [32mINFO[0m |     
2026-01-30 10:27:18 | [32mINFO[0m |     Joke 2 is significantly stronger. The escalating language ("soaring tensions," "fraying ties," "world on edge") immediately establishes a comedic contrast with the trivial reason for the outrage – souvenir keychains and a lack of texting etiquette. The "since last Tuesday!" line is a good, quick bit of absurdity. The specificity of Brenda and Kevin adds to the humor, making it feel more like a real, observed annoyance blown out of proportion. It commits fully to the bit and feels more natural and surprising. While still verbose, it's more effective in its delivery.
2026-01-30 10:27:18 | [32mINFO[0m |     
2026-01-30 10:27:18 | [32mINFO[0m |     Joke 1 fails on several counts: surprise, economy, and the laugh test. Joke 2 succeeds on surprise, naturalness, and has a much higher chance of eliciting a laugh.
